Z||000006||GoCartGuy||03-10-2001||02:08 AM||||I'm working on designing my speaker set up and was looking for some feed back on an idea I had.  First off is the subs, found a truck box set from Pioneer (200 watt a piece with a sweet 2 in tweeter).  Since we all know space is limited I had a revelutionary idea, we all realize that base should be felt as well as heard, so why not mount them where we feel it best, in the seats.  I'm planning on cutting out the back of the seats and mounting the boxes into the rear wall part way.  My other idea was rather than using the dash speakers for mid range to use those two channels for free standing 6x9's mounted at the clothing hooks.  Still deciding on the amp.  Let me know what you all think, I'm kinda new the the "sound in small spaces" arena.  Formerly owned a pick-up with extended cab...too bad with all the speakers it only sat 2.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000007||KRMFiero||03-10-2001||08:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by c m west:<BR><B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cwestco.com/Interior/Int_gif/Console2_500.jpg">  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would love to have that, but for 300$ i dont know, i have gray interier, do you offer a gray color?  if it was like maybe 200$ maybe even 250$  I might buy it but as nice as it looks itf 300$ just for a box, thats alot of money.<P>Kyle<P>btw.  <A HREF="http://www.subbox.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.subbox.com</A>   -they also sell a sub box for fiers for about 300$<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||03-10-2001||07:20 PM||||Hey GoCart, at the risk of sounding discouraging, sounds like you got a lot of butchering in mind for your car. I really do encourage you to at leas scrounge around the junkyard and take some measurements. The mods you describe would kill a lot of resale value if I were coming looking to buy. Also mounting the boxes in the seat would kill the high tones out of the tweeters. And I can't think of any time i'd want boxes of speakers precariously mounted over my head. Not very safe.<BR>I'd say, get the very best speakers you can afford for the stock locations, get good amps to drive them, and think about adding a sub. I can tell you the method I used is VERY effective!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||c m west||03-10-2001||07:49 PM||||for $300 it comes wrapped in vinyl of your descresion, as well as all cutouts for speaker and hardware. This unit has been featured in Auto Sound Magazine and has had great reviews from those who have heard it<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000010||GoCartGuy||03-11-2001||11:04 PM||||Hey Stimpy, I was a little concerned about the highs also, but a friend suggested something else, mounting the subs similar to the stock style behind the passenger seat, but behind both, and setting the tweeters into the supposed glove box.  As far as resale value, I'm not gettin rid of this ever, if possible.  I'll be pimpin it at age 35 with my kid in the passenger seat.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
